    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0476" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg466"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/2–248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-02-02T12:00:00+08:00">February 2,
                        1948—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 2—2:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>195. In considering our 181, January 29, 6 p.m., Department may wish to consult
                    our despatches 1144, December 6, 1947<anchor n="47" xml:id="d397-f1"/> and 28,
                    January <pb facs="0477" n="467" xml:id="pg467"/> 23, 1948<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d397-f2"/> on method of assisting Chinese to meet practical military
                    problems confronting them.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
